WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.334
Step 1. Open the pharmacy location from Services.

1.2
00:00:03.334 --> 00:00:07.992
Here you dispense medicines to a patient who has no prescription for them.

1.3
00:00:07.992 --> 00:00:12.773
Care remembers the pharmacy location you open here, and bills at it.

2.1
00:00:12.773 --> 00:00:15.079
Step 2. Start a new dispense.

2.2
00:00:15.079 --> 00:00:19.119
Select New Dispense at the top of the Prescription Queue.

2.3
00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:22.030
Care asks you to select a patient.

3.1
00:00:22.030 --> 00:00:23.983
Step 3. Find the patient.

3.2
00:00:23.983 --> 00:00:28.547
Search by phone number or by an identifier, and select the patient.

3.3
00:00:28.547 --> 00:00:38.876
If Care asks you to verify the patient's identity, enter the year of birth.

4.1
00:00:38.876 --> 00:00:44.055
Step 4. Proceed to dispense. Care shows the patient's name in the sheet.

4.2
00:00:44.055 --> 00:00:48.799
Select Proceed to Dispense, and Care opens the patient's page.

5.1
00:00:48.799 --> 00:00:51.100
Step 5. Select the encounter.

5.2
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:55.699
On the Encounters tab, select Dispense Medicine on the encounter.

5.3
00:00:55.699 --> 00:01:00.868
Care opens Bill Medications for that encounter, with no medicines.

6.1
00:01:00.868 --> 00:01:02.903
Step 6. Add the medicines.

6.2
00:01:02.903 --> 00:01:08.191
Search for the product in Add Medication, and set the Frequency and Duration.

6.3
00:01:08.191 --> 00:01:11.212
Care selects lots for the Required Quantity,

6.4
00:01:11.212 --> 00:01:30.525
and adds the medicine under Other Items.

7.1
00:01:30.525 --> 00:01:32.534
Step 7. Bill the medicines.

7.2
00:01:32.534 --> 00:01:36.246
Check the Estimated Total, and then select Bill Selected.

7.3
00:01:36.246 --> 00:01:39.177
Care creates the dispense order and opens it,

7.4
00:01:39.177 --> 00:01:42.869
with the payment sheet when it issued an invoice.
